{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335523Z","id":"fae90a18f682ff1b8e278c1274fa4eb28f51af8af9c154609fed1497dc3cc51b","body":{"detail":"Not taken: a PWA cannot start or keep a local clax daemon, so the store, db rules and comment pipeline would need a server off the device, against the goal that only the LLM call leaves it; its speech input and multi-touch handling also vary by browser. The design keeps the existing shell as the in-app WebView content, so a PWA would reuse most of it later.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"e3a11603e09bfdece7b2ccf5e72f96e01862903cefc9b3fbe2e1c8cc38245b60"},"summary":"Ship Clax as a PWA instead of a Flutter app","tags":["revisit:iOS is wanted without an App Store build, or the daemon can live off the device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335651Z","id":"0fc6c34c61dd01bb86ff7806d993397112011851f4c5f54fa578ba4c86450da1","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the page contract, window.claude capabilities, the bridge's comment anchoring and clips, and the db live in HTML/JS today (web/bridge, web/shell); rfw would need a second contract, a second anchoring scheme and a second agent prompt. Cost accepted: WebView start-up is part of say-to-usable.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"cee92505ec7d5d075b3fec57e5f6eed3fd4d4c0b6fdf1367d36bdd63854a62d7"},"summary":"Render generated apps as native widgets with rfw (Remote Flutter Widgets) instead of HTML in a WebView","tags":["revisit:measured WebView start-up exceeds half of say-to-usable, or home-screen widgets need native rendering","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335697Z","id":"b7dc250b3199309815c0eff2ae1b2e0bb0af486962b69969f53938d2e10d0eb9","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it would duplicate crates/clax-core semantics (db rules and levels, feedback tiers and resends, versions and blobs, the event stream) and drift from them; the cross-compiled clax runs unchanged on aarch64-linux-android (spike: 27.9 MB stripped, libc/libm/libdl only).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":40},"end":{"line":40},"content_hash":"cdf23135b8bd78aecf6bcc42163fad6f428819ce6a44c56a062d3684939fb8fb"},"summary":"Reimplement the store and routes in Dart instead of embedding clax","tags":["revisit:the child daemon cannot be kept alive on Android and the in-process FFI build is also ruled out","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335775Z","id":"bdf98fc2e010c7f78ec92b0b4d0d58f763e1cc0eb113b23212505e922741c3f0","body":{"detail":"Not taken: an exported entry point needs no_mangle, which is unsafe in edition 2024 while the workspace forbids unsafe_code (Cargo.toml); a daemon panic or abort would take the app down; global tracing initialisation and set_web_dist prevent restarting the daemon inside one process; and it adds a second build system. Benefit forgone: no Android 12+ phantom-process kills of a background child.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":88},"content_hash":"1ebe95c0ae75dd74aba0e180c6c1e6746b6ff5c464a73171b43604bf5845af3a"},"summary":"Run the daemon in-process as a cdylib through FFI instead of a supervised child process","tags":["revisit:on a device, Android kills the child daemon in the background on more than 1 in 10 resumes","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335820Z","id":"6ed78cebf1f606dad86414bbf4cd9098f2f66f07b2de7c9f3a8fc11d5968bf13","body":{"detail":"Not taken: flutter_inappwebview's last release is 6.1.5 (2024-10); webview_flutter 4.14.1 (2026-07) supports android and macos and provides JavaScriptChannel, runJavaScript and navigation delegates, which is all the app surface needs.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":354},"end":{"line":357},"content_hash":"a1389b71e22eb9a3c06b53ea1fb92820f8128d35d74dee4e79af9d1d547005eb"},"summary":"Use flutter_inappwebview instead of webview_flutter","tags":["revisit:webview_flutter lacks an API the app needs (touch interception, custom schemes, cookie control)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335860Z","id":"1092ee5d3774754c26b106308f154851376b86dee4562c90920f9dc326478bcb","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the page is a cross-origin iframe inside the shell, so the bridge in every page would have to watch two-touch gestures and forward them through the shell to the host, and a page's own touch handlers could swallow them. A Flutter Listener sees every pointer before the platform view without entering the gesture arena. Unverified on a device; the edge handle is the fallback.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":358},"end":{"line":363},"content_hash":"03a0b6dfec2550f3d50eb8cdf781ec39a414d9cec96d2d1d785480bfa4527fde"},"summary":"Detect the two-finger swipe in page JavaScript (the bridge) instead of a Flutter Listener","tags":["revisit:on an Android device the Listener does not receive the WebView's two-finger pointers","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335908Z","id":"ba6bac0ea917fcc8339cee830a26fa5700b18381daba10151e7e2fff2896f9bf","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the pick needs user activation in the frame either way, and the bridge renders the clip only after the shell composer's textarea has focus (clax:composer-ready); a Flutter composer would carry PNGs up to 5 MiB over the JavaScript channel and reimplement the anchor, the wait for the screenshot and the post. Cost accepted: typing uses the WebView's keyboard handling.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":433},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"008d31bb2c941f25f04967ec5508377b5377059201ff764b85bc8cb72af3d88a"},"summary":"Render the comment composer in Flutter instead of the shell","tags":["revisit:the WebView composer's keyboard behaviour on Android blocks typed comments","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.335944Z","id":"8966525add808207f2411a04464dc3fce82ff6bb0113fd85f5db46ca23e576e3","body":{"detail":"The stated shape for MessagesApiBackend is one forced tool carrying the edit schema. Forced tool_choice ({\"type\": \"tool\"} or \"any\") returns 400 on claude-opus-5-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5, so this design sends the same schema as output_config.format (json_schema), which every offered model supports, and keeps one schema for both backends. Recommendation: keep structured output. Alternative: a strict tool with tool_choice auto plus a prompt instruction.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":290},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"c86c9ace024ddad2af9bdc1ae0990c6efdb66ec77350bace6ac2f2dd6126d296"},"summary":"Messages API backend uses structured output, not one forced tool","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.336011Z","id":"92ee4c3fd18d7507db6422cf4d1bc57fce807239755bd32d3fcba0736e43928e","body":{"detail":"Chosen for say-to-usable and long-press-to-landed speed; app quality may be lower than claude-sonnet-5-5. Settings offer Sonnet 5.5 and Opus 5.5. Recommendation: keep Haiku 5.5 as the default until the live runs' timings and results are compared with Sonnet 5.5 at effort low.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":308},"end":{"line":310},"content_hash":"32c60d502ab5589380717b4c1888d78b211139389f16c216d18df875063b350c"},"summary":"Default model claude-haiku-5-5 at effort low","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.336050Z","id":"51f0d0679d13293353f930eb4e767ca3ba85dee285a9ca821021a8dd33ed290c","body":{"detail":"Loopback is shared by every app on an Android device. Unauthenticated reads (artifacts, content, view-level documents) are open to them, and GET /api/token answers a loopback request with a local Host header and Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, which a non-browser client can send, giving full owner access. v1 accepts this on the owner's phone. Recommendation: before anyone else installs the app, add a serve option that disables /api/token and have the Flutter host hand the token and event cookies to the WebView; and require the token for reads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":511},"end":{"line":517},"content_hash":"5f5bf7fe7c2cc252e924221f3089e0247787f070dc0467d77e70a7fc0ab01e33"},"summary":"Other Android apps can reach the embedded daemon and fetch its token","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.336085Z","id":"c1f270098a78753e9785932648b3146b0a4d482bc5ac252a31bdd7a46e389d27","body":{"detail":"When the person asks for an app that shows another app's data, the agent declares db.read and the page asks the owner once on first read (Allow / Don't allow). The loop could instead PUT the grant itself, since the owner's own request caused it. Conservative choice taken: always ask. Recommendation: auto-grant only for reads the person's own New request named, if the prompt proves a friction point in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":394},"end":{"line":399},"content_hash":"d03b7f4d951532ee0ec60acc1b2c27a9a873735a9ec6fd2ef72dfc3553272141"},"summary":"No automatic read grant when the agent builds an app that reads another app","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:29:30.336119Z","id":"f998fa52f40b75533c8c72437524c812f3087d1db58a73a94467fb9c1d1ff041","body":{"detail":"A sandboxed process cannot exec ~/.local/bin/claude or read its login, so ClaudeCliBackend is offered only when APP_SANDBOX_CONTAINER_ID is absent, and DebugProfile.entitlements drops app-sandbox. Release.entitlements keeps the sandbox (network.server, network.client, audio input) as distribution requires. Recommendation: keep; desktop use of the Claude CLI stays a developer build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":147},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"bc0f84b5e01e7f739b875893a0c647772af19a9f4a9f6f7cf8d9081827f38054"},"summary":"macOS debug builds run without the App Sandbox so claude -p can be started","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333473Z","id":"58e7c6489cc859943bdcd56f6ec3c186063e8d3697909b886bed37646c62e921","body":{"detail":"As built (commit 31fdb579, web/bridge/src/protocol.ts clax:welcome), the app shell asks for the restore by sending restoreScroll: <y> in the welcome it sends the newer version's document (with app: true); there is no clax:restore-scroll message. The message's handler alone cost 22 gzip bytes of the eager bridge, which was then over its 5501-byte budget, and the welcome orders the restore after the caps part that holds scroll.ts has loaded. After the deadline the restore scrolls as far as the document reaches rather than giving up (commit e1f1919d). Line 218 and plan Task W2 (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-12-flutter-app.md:632) still name clax:restore-scroll.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"7535e07684a3ad1b99f2ae6c4bb6862574ca65a14394f42840edd22637b37975"},"suggested_fix":"W2: include restoreScroll (the last clax:scroll y for the file) in the welcome after auto-follow loads the newer version. D1: document the welcome field in docs/contract.md.","summary":"The scroll restore is the welcome's restoreScroll field, not a clax:restore-scroll message","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:17:56.333515Z","id":"9a3a621efff3b3e2b68c1d67695d021ee38f8e7c09783406e54eede734baae63","body":{"detail":"As built (commit ef912931, web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts), selectstart and contextmenu are cancelled only while LongPress.holding, and the only style added in comment mode is -webkit-touch-callout:none. user-select:none for the whole mode, as this text says, broke mouse drag-select comments and Option+drag widening on desktop (e2e/area.spec.ts) and right-click menus.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":256},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"0302e7de62756cab5d5a31405a0ba81a54f1c584664a65f1cf9fc637d1c7ed91"},"summary":"The selection guard applies only while a finger is held, not for the whole of comment mode","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152862Z","id":"206f70b6c8193b45b2199c6569cef42e1a3fd4cefc1b22a15e1ee3b11f8a367e","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts sends restoreScroll in the first welcome after auto-follow; no clax:restore-scroll exists. Spec §3.4/§3.5 and plan Task W2 still name clax:restore-scroll; D1 documents the welcome field.","kind":"comment","references":"58e7c6489cc859943bdcd56f6ec3c186063e8d3697909b886bed37646c62e921","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"7535e07684a3ad1b99f2ae6c4bb6862574ca65a14394f42840edd22637b37975"},"summary":"The shell side is built on restoreScroll in the welcome (bba79ce3); the spec text and docs/contract.md still need the change","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:31:23.488475Z","id":"dd772516a6fc210f2f5c18935f37a3b254146f4de504ebf7919bd94114b5b443","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ac6b3f7d","summary":"The spec's 3.5 selection guard now says selectstart and contextmenu are cancelled only while a finger is held and that comment mode adds only -webkit-touch-callout:none, with why; docs/contract.md 'Comments and feedback' says the same.","supersedes":"9a3a621efff3b3e2b68c1d67695d021ee38f8e7c09783406e54eede734baae63","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:31:23.488820Z","id":"4a0a8230c2cff8bdca61bb200354285e007c8325b88235d0663ee195c82a5fb2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ac6b3f7d","summary":"The spec's 3.4 and 3.5 and docs/contract.md ('The Clax app', Auto-follow) now describe the welcome's restoreScroll, first welcome only, and say there is no clax:restore-scroll message; grep -n restore-scroll on both files finds only that statement.","supersedes":"58e7c6489cc859943bdcd56f6ec3c186063e8d3697909b886bed37646c62e921","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.562652Z","id":"3433c4b86d36044bddc0074c98d608fb1bb42844776fc55d553b21db56d33dc0","body":{"detail":"Not taken: `clax mcp` has no drafts and no render tool, so the desktop agent could not check its work; its publish and db tools write the live app directly, bypassing the change ledger, pinned writes and restore-on-refusal that live in the Dart Toolbox (R§4.5); and the shim ends its session when its transport closes, which would end the app's own session if it registered with the app's install ID. An MCP server the app serves keeps one Toolbox for both backends.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"d5038f242eff858d7941d199e44ca087476e74399191a7e3f33fd6df5d0d518b"},"summary":"Give claude -p the tools through `clax mcp` pointed at the embedded daemon","tags":["revisit:clax mcp gains drafts, a render tool and ledger-aware writes, or the CLI becomes a path on the phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.562767Z","id":"b495805f8f9eab9edf20a7c596f39289d02e855c44e0a36745e5fd347c624c2d","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the daemon has no browser engine on Android, and shipping one is out of reach; the app already hosts WebViews.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":313},"end":{"line":345},"content_hash":"00efee97cf59ce4c3b618a766a7f293fae30149882cd0faf132954460ba8d597"},"summary":"Render drafts on the daemon with a headless browser","tags":["revisit:the daemon ships a browser engine on the desktop and renders become a bottleneck in the app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.562813Z","id":"6384592063476766e5e7465e61408f4983e2a0e95f90af1c713d3d8cb1af1d0f","body":{"detail":"Not taken: webview_flutter exposes no snapshot API, so it needs Kotlin and Swift code and an attached, drawn view; the bridge's clip renderer (web/bridge/src/clip.ts, modern-screenshot) already runs in-page on both platforms. Cost: canvas, video and cross-origin images may render blank or as placeholders.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":331},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"d379cc9e1695da3b3ac448d5feb71222c5413495f2d570fe02433f3a2b11ef31"},"summary":"Take the inspection screenshot natively (Android View.draw, WKWebView.takeSnapshot) instead of the bridge's DOM render","tags":["revisit:the live check (Task L2) or device use shows inspections missing canvas or images in ways that mislead the agent","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.562853Z","id":"7e49c7588c1fd9b3af055bc9edc6643ebec3b713bc117f3d235c79e3a7d6f9b5","body":{"detail":"Not taken: half-done work would become versions, auto-follow would reload the app under the person mid-change (against RO2: the current version stays usable until the change lands), and version history would fill with intermediate states.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"8030e69289e956d05025dd32f31d08e66d921218d34d49f9ca06f810bc81d8b1"},"summary":"Publish each clean render as a new version while the run goes","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to see a new app or change live in place before it is finished","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.562892Z","id":"a06a23a4159909bf5edc56b0c86e4a9477c3dd063ef4483f9247b304e375d03f","body":{"detail":"Not taken: queries and onSnapshot run on the daemon, so an overlay would need a second query engine in the shell to merge reads; a hidden artifact with copied documents reuses the page contract, bridge and db unchanged and keeps render writes away from the app.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":312},"content_hash":"f625034b1c86343bc5f867433ad6f3f60d5ecd88998113e9cf68d27976e0de6c"},"summary":"Render drafts with an in-memory db overlay in the shell instead of hidden draft artifacts with a document copy","tags":["revisit:the document copy is truncated often (docs_truncated) or copying slows renders noticeably","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.562929Z","id":"0159bc17534f484ca1c6bf6b3f2c2da5b6acde6fe7ea8cae1aa14d72f4b11805","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the reply and the resolve travel with the version in finish so the change ledger (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/ledger.dart) can replay them after a crash; separate tools would let a reply land without its version or the other way round.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":116},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"c53779c24f7085bfee50d7eb5e6109edaab8de325cfc91c83923756e8469dbbd"},"summary":"Give the agent separate reply_to_thread and resolve tools","tags":["revisit:agents need to reply mid-run, for example on long changes or to report progress in the thread","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.563003Z","id":"de0c7a5985efee478adc085921c422af1ec17d7068568a93b5c22fd21b74c05c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the agent never said it was done; publishing work it did not finish could change the app in ways the person did not ask for. Retry runs the change again with a fresh budget.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":220},"content_hash":"e3dad70639af14220b03cf68f12bf8472657a17d0f0037b8d11150592c762074"},"summary":"Publish a clean, rendered draft when a hard cap stops the run","tags":["revisit:agent timings show hard-cap failures whose last render was clean and changed the requested thing","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.563060Z","id":"f98462c0c1ced2de9ad57542ae0ba5778ad4e6831b068a3e635b7159a4288e5c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it needs a scroll loop in the bridge driven by timers while a finger rests, and the selection and area code to follow scroll offsets; picks on a phone are mostly within one screen.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":488},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"442ef2d032da459dff5bb39ec866a9fb22bd15ff3b85636072dfbcbefe6b82ca"},"summary":"Auto-scroll the page when a hold-drag reaches the top or bottom edge","tags":["revisit:the owner tries to select text or draw an area larger than the viewport","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.563104Z","id":"02e0f9f760d5b0bd9b260eaa604a07d1daceeb08d6097cae3c2f7ee2582bead2","body":{"detail":"Not taken: two agent paths double what must be tested and kept in step, and the owner chose the tool loop that checks its work (R§1 RO4) for changes too.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":402},"end":{"line":413},"content_hash":"73d0ad1b05da784f4b36d3acb027b0fceffbed379c65e6085c822db528b4aed1"},"summary":"Keep the single structured-output call as a fast path for small changes","tags":["revisit:the live check (Task L2) measures long-press->landed above the 20 s target for one-element changes","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.563182Z","id":"d624da2df950affa2630326c191c6c3684779c9ec26472e93b7c1ec2de744df3","body":{"detail":"The owner's round-2 decision says `claude -p` gets the same tools via the Clax MCP server. This design serves the Toolbox itself over MCP on loopback (R§4.3), because `clax mcp` has no drafts or render and its writes bypass the change ledger (see the alternative record on these lines). Choice taken until answered: the app's own MCP server. Options: (a) keep it; (b) extend `clax mcp` with drafts, a render request relayed to the app, and ledger-aware writes (large Rust and relay work).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":195},"content_hash":"d5038f242eff858d7941d199e44ca087476e74399191a7e3f33fd6df5d0d518b"},"summary":"Q1: desktop claude -p gets the tools from an MCP server the app serves, not from `clax mcp`","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.563230Z","id":"bc835104e353dedd1effc869418f012f9efb6672fe1803501445bc2f688c9b3f","body":{"detail":"Gate in R§4.5. Cost: about one model turn and 1-2 s of rendering per change, pushing long-press->landed from ~5 s (single call, L1) toward the 20 s target. Choice taken until answered: mandatory. Options: (a) mandatory; (b) the agent decides when to render; the gate only refuses after a render that showed errors.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"e53c450aa4dccbe302f34284dc54f7082397617679ef8bf6f692cd91068b822c"},"summary":"Q2: every finish that publishes must follow a render of that exact draft","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.563268Z","id":"1b8e45848b376f184267be94f8f23ea6c038a25e3812fd7e09ec7ea024bca3e9","body":{"detail":"R§4.4. On claude-haiku-5-5 the cost cap is far above a normal run; it matters for claude-sonnet-5-5 and claude-opus-5-5. At a hard cap the run gives up and the person sees Retry. Choice taken until answered: these values. Options: other values; a per-day cost cap; publishing a clean draft at the cap (alternative record on 213:220).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":196},"end":{"line":220},"content_hash":"75b0e5d37e562f1c47e5e065a464f7dc0156683933b957362b2bd47a3161b3e2"},"summary":"Q3: run caps (14/12 turns, 4 renders, 60k/40k output tokens, $1.00, 6/5 min) and nothing published at a hard cap","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:22:28.563304Z","id":"cc0f4ba1446b4051e843d180a9ddeb1bd9f47fc518300949e6eeaacb7c3de40b","body":{"detail":"R§8. While parked the threads carry a reply saying a question is waiting; the late answer on the feedback poll runs the change again. A new app waits up to 5 minutes on the making screen. Choice taken until answered: 60 s then park. Options: wait longer while the foreground service holds the run (Android allows a dataSync service; battery cost); never ask on a change, always take the recommended option and say so in the reply.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":429},"end":{"line":449},"content_hash":"c69039c8fbfe177f4520c15978015d5683605d41ec4d4662eb4309dbc396e8f1"},"summary":"Q4: ask_owner on a change waits 60 s, then parks the change until the answer","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:kesling@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.285774Z","id":"ccbb390cd152085dd37ded473e34bfa09a6904d23cad072a782cec4d79c9c780","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer (2026-10-12): \"Don't overcomplicate this at the moment, let's ship a better app.\" The spec carries it as RA1, R§4.3.","kind":"comment","references":"d624da2df950affa2630326c191c6c3684779c9ec26472e93b7c1ec2de744df3","summary":"Decided: no MCP server and no claude -p tool loop this round; both platforms run the Dart Messages API tool loop, and ClaudeCliBackend stays the desktop's single-call fallback without an API key.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:kesling@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.285825Z","id":"47fc0696f9e384a1406f149123206f22a1e77f8092ba9435a27b3963f822c03b","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer (2026-10-12): \"Always render first.\" The spec carries it as RA2, R§4.5.","kind":"comment","references":"bc835104e353dedd1effc869418f012f9efb6672fe1803501445bc2f688c9b3f","summary":"Decided: every finish that publishes follows a render of that exact draft.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:kesling@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.285850Z","id":"4a7b6f7302e84336f16772e06db2d769fa241f9ed56feeb14be3d55dc6206a96","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer (2026-10-12): \"The experience should be iterate, smooth, and quick.\" The spec carries it as RA3, R§4.4.","kind":"comment","references":"1b8e45848b376f184267be94f8f23ea6c038a25e3812fd7e09ec7ea024bca3e9","summary":"Decided: small caps sized so a typical change lands well under 30 s on Haiku (change: 6 turns, 2 renders, 20,000 output tokens, 45 s; new app: 8, 3, 32,000, 90 s); at a cap the last draft that rendered without errors is published saying it stopped early, else nothing is published and Retry is offered; the cost cap ($0.50) stays as a safety net.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:kesling@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.285876Z","id":"3996cc6bd3499e4e3cf38363a460e755df939681fa376709f9fc904779383ab3","body":{"detail":"The owner's answer (2026-10-12): \"Look at how Clax does elicitation.\" The spec carries it as RA4, R§8 and R§10.2.","kind":"comment","references":"cc0f4ba1446b4051e843d180a9ddeb1bd9f47fc518300949e6eeaacb7c3de40b","summary":"Decided: the agent asks with Clax's own ask (its arguments, result, session routes and late answers), and the owner answers in the shell's question card; no parallel question model.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.298627Z","id":"2d3555e91dba9e907592b3e356e05948eb0d62169bbb921b05d9ba8433ce02cb","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Obsolete: the owner chose this path (RA3 in R§1); R§4.4 now publishes the last clean draft at a cap.","supersedes":"de0c7a5985efee478adc085921c422af1ec17d7068568a93b5c22fd21b74c05c","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.299217Z","id":"40beae8c703c93cc4626b562fdfa345b9457239addd06b1cf30bbd2cec622ed6","body":{"detail":"Not taken: half-done work would become versions, auto-follow would reload the app under the person mid-change (against RO2: the current version stays usable until the change lands), and version history would fill with intermediate states.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":108},"content_hash":"275cf16fbccf9f77116d9b6523876e6ef615a88b0f62fd64dc31580be663e69a"},"summary":"Publish each clean render as a new version while the run goes","supersedes":"7e49c7588c1fd9b3af055bc9edc6643ebec3b713bc117f3d235c79e3a7d6f9b5","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to see a new app or change live in place before it is finished","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.299708Z","id":"a1a4f40421d5fb076e8c2d2db55f17083d7b3b9ce49ff363e4471cf1ac58414a","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the reply and the resolve travel with the version in finish so the change ledger (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/ledger.dart) can replay them after a crash; separate tools would let a reply land without its version or the other way round.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":144},"content_hash":"5bb5bcef173a931e8a75761c892cbc1aa6664b351839807ed94b9bbf628ef8a0"},"summary":"Give the agent separate reply_to_thread and resolve tools","supersedes":"0159bc17534f484ca1c6bf6b3f2c2da5b6acde6fe7ea8cae1aa14d72f4b11805","tags":["revisit:agents need to reply mid-run, for example on long changes or to report progress in the thread","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.300195Z","id":"506564d5b4d0a5ff91691fee4b367c3a180a2afe1975c5be51f446391208ed8b","body":{"detail":"Not taken: `clax mcp` has no drafts and no render tool, so the desktop agent could not check its work; its publish and db tools write the live app directly, bypassing the change ledger, pinned writes and restore-on-refusal that live in the Dart Toolbox (R§4.5); and the shim ends its session when its transport closes, which would end the app's own session if it registered with the app's install ID. An MCP server the app serves keeps one Toolbox for both backends.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"89c33e6f34d94ae5ab3fdfd6cbdb1f0b315604bc2bc0c95ae6501b1d98aa0fa8"},"summary":"Give claude -p the tools through `clax mcp` pointed at the embedded daemon","supersedes":"3433c4b86d36044bddc0074c98d608fb1bb42844776fc55d553b21db56d33dc0","tags":["revisit:clax mcp gains drafts, a render tool and ledger-aware writes, or the CLI becomes a path on the phone","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.300678Z","id":"12b0bd7f34cf8b74dd1b21348255c7c49f292788febacade9d7a16de463ec9da","body":{"detail":"Not taken: queries and onSnapshot run on the daemon, so an overlay would need a second query engine in the shell to merge reads; a hidden artifact with copied documents reuses the page contract, bridge and db unchanged and keeps render writes away from the app.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":336},"content_hash":"f625034b1c86343bc5f867433ad6f3f60d5ecd88998113e9cf68d27976e0de6c"},"summary":"Render drafts with an in-memory db overlay in the shell instead of hidden draft artifacts with a document copy","supersedes":"a06a23a4159909bf5edc56b0c86e4a9477c3dd063ef4483f9247b304e375d03f","tags":["revisit:the document copy is truncated often (docs_truncated) or copying slows renders noticeably","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.301165Z","id":"e26f2503635a3dbeb18cda1a0738d1e7943de76a33ad65611f9924de6c8de8c9","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the daemon has no browser engine on Android, and shipping one is out of reach; the app already hosts WebViews.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":337},"end":{"line":371},"content_hash":"bf7fbd3b512a2e7d61e8877306f6098e99b78301a438133ffacafb4de98acd29"},"summary":"Render drafts on the daemon with a headless browser","supersedes":"b495805f8f9eab9edf20a7c596f39289d02e855c44e0a36745e5fd347c624c2d","tags":["revisit:the daemon ships a browser engine on the desktop and renders become a bottleneck in the app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.301646Z","id":"1222ad164ba321fbeb9a3069be7d9c2a457b066995f07e9ff5209642a78597a0","body":{"detail":"Not taken: webview_flutter exposes no snapshot API, so it needs Kotlin and Swift code and an attached, drawn view; the bridge's clip renderer (web/bridge/src/clip.ts, modern-screenshot) already runs in-page on both platforms. Cost: canvas, video and cross-origin images may render blank or as placeholders.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":357},"end":{"line":359},"content_hash":"ad398447a8d9e88dac815863aa70004fe69495052349ae415ac7fdf7cb0b4173"},"summary":"Take the inspection screenshot natively (Android View.draw, WKWebView.takeSnapshot) instead of the bridge's DOM render","supersedes":"6384592063476766e5e7465e61408f4983e2a0e95f90af1c713d3d8cb1af1d0f","tags":["revisit:the live check (Task L2) or device use shows inspections missing canvas or images in ways that mislead the agent","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.302133Z","id":"41c8027aced2cad2c05561edc7577c6642f27c96cf0ef25f324854ff724697de","body":{"detail":"Not taken for the Messages API path: two agent paths there double what must be tested, and the owner chose the tool loop that checks its work (R§1 RO4). The single structured call does stay on the desktop without an API key (R§4.3).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":428},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"8d4e9127cd1c93a2a9e60e8b807367832aeaf8980a517d68db792640b4e9d938"},"summary":"Keep the single structured-output call as a fast path for small changes","supersedes":"02e0f9f760d5b0bd9b260eaa604a07d1daceeb08d6097cae3c2f7ee2582bead2","tags":["revisit:the live check (Task L2) measures long-press->landed above the 20 s target for one-element changes","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.302625Z","id":"d9d039853c9a8c5b6758737febf7dd7b17c7691089145ac1868f11a9b8d98874","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it needs a scroll loop in the bridge driven by timers while a finger rests, and the selection and area code to follow scroll offsets; picks on a phone are mostly within one screen.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":548},"end":{"line":548},"content_hash":"442ef2d032da459dff5bb39ec866a9fb22bd15ff3b85636072dfbcbefe6b82ca"},"summary":"Auto-scroll the page when a hold-drag reaches the top or bottom edge","supersedes":"f98462c0c1ced2de9ad57542ae0ba5778ad4e6831b068a3e635b7159a4288e5c","tags":["revisit:the owner tries to select text or draw an area larger than the viewport","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.303097Z","id":"e81caef99e57f2c9da45c16e7a56d89a36d2d8bdbb1752e776237cf7fc95d349","body":{"detail":"Dropped this round by the owner (RA1): both platforms run the Dart Messages API tool loop, and the desktop without a key keeps today's single structured call through ClaudeCliBackend, with no render and no ask. The design it would have had: the app serves the run's Toolbox over Streamable HTTP on 127.0.0.1 with a bearer token, and claude -p gets --mcp-config with only that server, --strict-mcp-config, --tools \"\", --allowedTools listing each tool, --safe-mode; the run's outcome is the Toolbox's finish or give_up.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"89c33e6f34d94ae5ab3fdfd6cbdb1f0b315604bc2bc0c95ae6501b1d98aa0fa8"},"summary":"Run claude -p as a tool loop on the desktop, with the Toolbox served as an MCP server on loopback (planned as Task A8)","tags":["revisit:the owner wants the tool loop on the desktop without an API key, on a Claude Code login","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:41:07.303142Z","id":"1fa4e2d5fba2189bc34434eab43a585652aa7c48a81887dd323f09fc4a925d1c","body":{"detail":"Not taken: the owner asked for Clax's own elicitation (RA4); the shell's QuestionCard.svelte already implements the question shape, multi-question navigation, previews, Other and Skip, and answers from the owner's browser record answered_via shell. A Flutter copy would be a second implementation to keep in step, and a token answer from Dart would record answered_via cli.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":622},"end":{"line":648},"content_hash":"9a696ef7c39b9ad2b2afbb7726c3673e60e22f86bc9ca9a85e0129259303c0c1"},"summary":"Answer the agent's questions in a Flutter copy of the question card","tags":["revisit:the WebView question sheet is slow to open or awkward with the phone keyboard","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:01:39.906752Z","id":"4a6405940f76fcd683fccde49129146c4d89e5c5ffd0355f05af58196b2434b7","body":{"detail":"Since 6c09b2d3, Store::may_read (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs:157) answers NotGranted for a draft reading any other artifact, and record 74b1b568 holds the consent-gated variant. The spec's 'Reads of other apps' bullet describes the earlier mapping of a draft to its app's grants, so a reader of the spec (and docs/contract.md, written from it) would expect renders to read other apps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":327},"content_hash":"b84000f2c053f85a0c1c60e7007a7ac8857b37f4947ff8a222af0b589ad63868"},"summary":"R§5.1 still says a draft reads other apps with the grants of `of`; Store::may_read now refuses every cross-app read by a draft","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:44:45.467562Z","id":"962e99525f3f559c969f3ac8e8a8d372b50aaca2ab14a8357a13a882f3474b4b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"92ee4c3fd18d7507db6422cf4d1bc57fce807239755bd32d3fcba0736e43928e","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-13): the default model for a new install is claude-sonnet-5-5.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:58:42.969632Z","id":"83406283775d36d674b24ab85d27cbee66679bcde15e3348221ed56e70566850","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9012afb7","summary":"Fixed in 9012afb7: defaultModel = 'claude-sonnet-5-5' in apps/clax_app/lib/platform/settings_store.dart (effort stays low, set per backend, not per model); a saved choice is kept. Spec §3.6 Models and D-2 updated. Tests in apps/clax_app/test/ui/settings_test.dart ('a missing file loads the defaults', 'an install that saved Haiku keeps it'): flutter test test/ui/settings_test.dart +17, All tests passed.","supersedes":"92ee4c3fd18d7507db6422cf4d1bc57fce807239755bd32d3fcba0736e43928e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:12:05.398939Z","id":"6aa28ceb63647ea69d4d38612b82456ac2d4a3b3cab47b6ad61d86292be7dd9f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:561af026","summary":"Fixed: clax serve --foreground --require-credential (crates/clax-server/src/auth.rs require_credential, wired in crates/clax-server/src/lib.rs wrap) answers 401 to every request without the bearer token, the key cookie clax_key_<port> or the owner/events cookie, GET /api/token included; the app's supervisor starts the daemon with it and WebViewAppSurface sets the key cookie before each load (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart, lib/ui/webview_surface.dart, lib/main.dart). Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server -p clax-cli: 973 passed, including integration api_locked (token route 401 with forged Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, artifact/list/shell/gallery reads 401 unauthenticated and 2xx with the token or key cookie, default daemon unchanged). Live debug daemon with the flag: GET /api/token with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin -> 401, with the key cookie -> 200; GET /api/artifacts/<id> -> 401, with bearer -> 200; /api/artifacts 401/200; /a/<id>?app=1 401/200 with key cookie. flutter test integration_test/locked_daemon_test.dart -d macos passes (and times out without the key cookie). Content by artifact ID stays open: waiver 114b967d.","supersedes":"51f0d0679d13293353f930eb4e767ca3ba85dee285a9ca821021a8dd33ed290c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.571564Z","id":"6b12264fa298ef94dd8d4c04ef4ed75f4d15c00bc9f34386d255f2061886c888","body":{"detail":"An update could carry only the files that changed since a named base version. Not taken: full bundles need no base on the recipient's side, verify the same way as a first install, and the files of a generated app are small (the 64 MiB cap is far above typical apps). A patch format would add a base-mismatch failure and a second verification path.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"a2f8837b8f205572b83987e7487203be10adaf3978933048de7a2c17319a4b65"},"summary":"Patch (delta) update bundles instead of full bundles","tags":["revisit:update bundles routinely exceed a few MiB, or people send updates over metered links and complain of size","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.571811Z","id":"f21ce6360220c49994ff2ab3910692b78e99fdd62cd364413581ad37061def7b","body":{"detail":"When a recipient's copy is modified, the agent could re-apply the recipient's comment threads (the change requests that produced their versions) onto the update, instead of the binary choice 'Update (replaces your changes)' / 'Keep mine (stop updates)' of section 3.3. Deferred, not rejected: it needs the agent, an API key on the recipient's side, and a check that the replay landed, which is a feature of its own.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"5d55ac578c22cf1d1f549ae5751f3b038af40345bbe6f30683c5359b7fe1c4ee"},"summary":"Replay the recipient's own change requests onto the author's new version with the agent","tags":["revisit:recipients who changed an installed app hit an update and choose between replace and keep more than occasionally","status:deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.571923Z","id":"00bd2c52c42dc836076a91c1c12b276dc57a2ee37c0a5e7df2ba019dbae9b910","body":{"detail":"Bundling in the daemon would let the CLI and the web gallery share apps too. Not taken: the signing key lives in the Flutter app's secure storage, the share sheet and file associations are the app's, and the daemon would need new Rust dependencies (a zip reader and Ed25519; ring is only transitive in Cargo.lock). Every route a bundle needs already exists (section 7).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":449},"end":{"line":483},"content_hash":"b436a50a0745ff043ccb34c0321f1c96f1070ded3cdf5ea027be08b6b33022e1"},"summary":"Daemon routes for export and import (GET /api/artifacts/<id>/bundle, POST /api/bundles)","tags":["revisit:the clax CLI or the web gallery needs to export or install a .clax bundle","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.572107Z","id":"be16086900ae0f8b420a0eb6368f00ad4aacee49ffb66fcbda1291e203b26b8f","body":{"detail":"The manifest could carry its own signature field, signed over a canonicalization of the rest. Not taken: the bundle signs the exact stored bytes of manifest.json (with a domain prefix) and keeps the signature in manifest.sig, so no canonical form has to be agreed between writers and readers, and capability declarations with arbitrary JSON numbers need no canonical number encoding.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":280},"end":{"line":297},"content_hash":"ab00bf011ffe81820496219df31303dedbfd0ec9d6ae856ab37ac341b97a9d38"},"summary":"Signature inside manifest.json over a canonical JSON form (JCS, RFC 8785)","tags":["revisit:a verifier outside this Dart code (another language, a server) must check bundles and wants a single self-contained manifest file","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.572222Z","id":"0eb806f137baa3c34eb08b21457245dcdccadab8281e4b15807e0dac47c9660c","body":{"detail":"A bundle's db.read names the author's artifact IDs. They could be rewritten to lineage IDs and mapped to the recipient's installed apps of those lineages. Not taken: it needs a mapping table, a consent story for reads across apps from different senders, and sets of apps travelling together. Section 4.4 strips both keys at export and refuses bundles that carry them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":271},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"63c296b30da591b224b2865980a04cf79b6fdbc6a43680e9706055dfc4fade74"},"summary":"Carry cross-app reads (db.read / db.share) in bundles, mapped by lineage","tags":["revisit:people share sets of apps that read each other's data, e.g. a tracker and its dashboard","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.572345Z","id":"5c8c276db40d59e3dd01b9b7786359e6a5e1db7987e0ac1dd3bfc3e846773041","body":{"detail":"Each install has its own Ed25519 key, so a person who reinstalls Clax or uses a second device cannot update apps they shared earlier: recipients get a separate app (threat T9). A synced or exportable key, or a rotation record signed by the old key, would fix it. Not taken for the prototype.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":299},"end":{"line":312},"content_hash":"8588ef3cfd073ff9f300083ba6ff92ee447efb8e56b08bafb565aeabcfd9b1c3"},"summary":"One author identity across a person's devices (key sync, backup or rotation)","tags":["revisit:one person uses Clax on two devices and wants to update a shared app from either, or reinstalls Clax after sharing apps","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.572471Z","id":"c9c15a4cb2e11f3ab733d4d0c8389e595fd2b03bef4a6b98563590a09145df23","body":{"detail":"The update check already migrates a copy of the recipient's documents in the draft; on a pass those documents could be written back to the live app, so the migration runs once and has been checked on exactly what lands. Not taken: the draft copy is capped (2,000 documents, 8 MiB) and goes stale if the app is written during the check, and no daemon route copies documents from a draft to its app. migrate.js must be idempotent instead.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":524},"end":{"line":528},"content_hash":"7007197cc9846eed06795c8540ea24eba415f5c490e8766a8d1f93bcc941ed2a"},"summary":"Copy the draft's migrated documents back into the live app instead of running migrate.js on the live app","tags":["revisit:a live migration fails after its check passed, or apps outgrow the draft copy's caps","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.572608Z","id":"85606187c51b443332d1c405de9da99e9732f07debe2ecd15857687dfc751d66","body":{"detail":"The install sheet lists what the app can ask for; pressing Install could grant net hosts, sample and device capabilities at once. Not taken: the existing per-use consent (once per app and capability) already applies to agent-made apps, keeps one consent model, and a capability the app never uses is never granted.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":536},"end":{"line":543},"content_hash":"b8e38a111dd3fdec5cee834128baa4764005553786609f6807893e6d6d298b79"},"summary":"Grant every declared capability at Install instead of first-use consent","tags":["revisit:people find first-use prompts in installed apps confusing after the install sheet already listed the capabilities","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.572713Z","id":"bdd57c66046dc6e226ebc6b15a90d1d752ef9ce74d413b1ccedbf709819ba2aa","body":{"detail":"An older signed bundle of the same lineage and key could install as a downgrade after a warning. Not taken: refusing makes a replayed old version (one with a known bug) unusable as an attack, and the recipient can return to any earlier version they had with the Versions tab.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":432},"end":{"line":432},"content_hash":"18e2bc89095ce9d9cc75e35638f64040735f502e802b50cfdef3f365ebaf08ec"},"summary":"Ask instead of refusing when a bundle is an older version of an installed app","tags":["revisit:an author's update is broken and recipients need the author's earlier version they never installed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:27:34.572813Z","id":"4a7d642f15b333520b6c8979ae37a81ecd7bdc35d24c1e1238b3d86141d1717f","body":{"detail":"Section 8.2 step 7 runs migrate.js on the live app after the check passed on a copy. If it fails (documents written after the copy, a bug the copy did not reach), the version is restored but the data is not: there is no document snapshot to restore. Accepted for the prototype: migrate.js must be idempotent, so the same update can be applied again, and the person is told documents may have changed.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":524},"end":{"line":528},"content_hash":"7007197cc9846eed06795c8540ea24eba415f5c490e8766a8d1f93bcc941ed2a"},"summary":"A live migrate.js run that fails part way leaves the documents it changed","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:32:40.096484Z","id":"304b654a25eab871a2aa05513f90aed5684edcb5550838928642fc3f44ebb326","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Obsolete: the owner ruled on 2026-10-13 that the live migrate.js run is snapshotted and a failure part way rolls back both the documents and the version (spec sections 8.2 step 7 and 8.4, threat T7), so no partial data change is left to accept.","supersedes":"4a7d642f15b333520b6c8979ae37a81ecd7bdc35d24c1e1238b3d86141d1717f","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:32:40.099511Z","id":"1a1f759394435028764a519d7a142b3694fd5026bca4703c723bf1074e667274","body":{"detail":"The update check already migrates a copy of the recipient's documents in the draft; on a pass those documents could be written back to the live app, so the migration runs once and has been checked on exactly what lands. Not taken: the draft copy is capped (2,000 documents, 8 MiB) and goes stale if the app is written during the check, and no daemon route copies documents from a draft to its app. Instead migrate.js runs on the live app under a document snapshot (section 8.4) that a failure restores.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":535},"end":{"line":541},"content_hash":"02219a34f89de9e40cc5e523caa9b8d45b9eb96c08c041e207696ee4fa86a21a"},"summary":"Copy the draft's migrated documents back into the live app instead of running migrate.js on the live app","supersedes":"c9c15a4cb2e11f3ab733d4d0c8389e595fd2b03bef4a6b98563590a09145df23","tags":["revisit:a live migration fails after its check passed, or apps outgrow the draft copy's caps","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:43:08.335403Z","id":"edbed304608c97ea5a8090b41c788d8b7f86fe5c79b957485d9d9a743594cba6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:67f7c452","summary":"R§5.1 now says a draft reads no other app's documents (Store::may_read answers not_granted, crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs:182-196), and docs/contract.md says so under Drafts and Reading another app's documents; scripts/test-plugins.sh and scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check pass","supersedes":"4a6405940f76fcd683fccde49129146c4d89e5c5ffd0355f05af58196b2434b7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:50:29.464282Z","id":"cef8501fe768ac1cdc2fb8dd5a7d00175339cd45127a725c91c1ee53e4dd62ed","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/data_tools.dart dataTools(api, fromBundle:) and apps/clax_app/lib/agent/prompt.dart firstChange/firstContinue/change(fromBundle:) enforce T2 (commit 44195628), and AgentRequest.fromBundle exists, but every caller passes the default false: apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart builds dataTools(_api) at line 962 and calls the PromptBuilder without fromBundle, and AgentLoop has no LineageStore to ask. §14 gives loop.dart (and the AgentLoop construction in lib/app.dart) to no task. Until AgentLoop looks up the app's lineage entry (from_bundle) per change and continue run and passes it to dataTools, the prompt builders and AgentRequest, an installed app's agent still sees the person's other apps and may read them with consent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":652},"end":{"line":653},"content_hash":"c291ed0247819d583da0f19cc0a34d7d5ec52d96646d41898d4a8bedd0daf8fc"},"suggested_fix":"Inject LineageStore (or a bool Function(String aid)) into AgentLoop; pass fromBundle at loop.dart's dataTools call, firstChange, firstContinue, change and AgentRequest.","summary":"No task wires fromBundle from the lineage store into the agent's runs","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:55:49.886885Z","id":"38174e98a5e9c1bb54053af786fc1f11bb3a97b6841d137d7db5370290f7dcb8","body":{"detail":"§4.2 says kit is the content hash (§4.5) of the files under kit/ alone, but not whether each line's path is the app path (kit/kit.js) or the path inside kit/ (kit.js). apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_writer.dart hashes the app paths, kit/ prefix kept. The field is informational and no reader checks it, so nothing breaks today; a second writer, or any later comparison of kit values, needs the spec to pick one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":267},"end":{"line":268},"content_hash":"ca0d035a5364efedb20b136f02cf19f151f821934ca2473aa9a5622762772469"},"summary":"The kit hash rule does not say whether paths keep their kit/ prefix","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:55:49.958440Z","id":"58dcc577e62d0ec6382fda66efc157b8d1789d8fa8d604c36929f12e9f5c66a8","body":{"detail":"§4.3 refuses a seed path under data/users/. The document path data/users (collection data, document users) is the owner's own document, not inside a per-viewer subtree, so apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/bundle_reader.dart isSeedPath accepts it and refuses only paths starting data/users/ (test: format_reader_test.dart 'data/users itself is a document of the owner, so it reads'). The rule also does not cover subtrees of a declared {self} rule (crates/clax-core/src/db.rs self_prefixes), which the daemon's draft copy also leaves out; a seed written by the exporter from the draft-copy read would not contain them, but a crafted bundle could seed them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":277},"end":{"line":280},"content_hash":"15b6153608f6f3dacd5f46b74d70d015c22e5130212f1fa5be9d8b9a450bbf61"},"summary":"Whether the seed may hold the document data/users itself is not stated","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:56:02.653148Z","id":"1f1b697699c94e795a7400926cc8062f0ff2df0df04975bac02bfedf2ae26a73","body":{"detail":"§8.1 step 2 compares the new version's content_sha256 with the manifest's and deletes the artifact on a mismatch, and step 4 deletes it on a failure in steps 1-3; §7 names only readFileBytes, FileEntry and entries. ClaxApi now has deleteArtifact (DELETE /api/artifacts/<aid>, an existing token route) and VersionInfo.contentSha256 (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart, models.dart); createDraft's files became optional (default empty) beside entries, so the test fakes overriding it in test/agent/worker_test.dart, test/agent/tools/finish_test.dart and render_tool_test.dart changed their signatures.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":480},"end":{"line":493},"content_hash":"1a0210ec4f99ce0405cc6c2858718b3d1af963dda9dd503165d7b09fb1d481ba"},"suggested_fix":"Add both entries to §7's list.","summary":"§7's ClaxApi list omits two entries §8.1 needs: deleteArtifact and VersionInfo.contentSha256","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:58:52.040340Z","id":"c0df38438bdc08693f6636279f9051c1ae5a59eb8a6a981fe409eefda4bbe0d5","body":{"detail":"Record 7658e09c (web/bridge/src/harness.ts:300-325) names the race: runMigration is ordered once the page has greeted, after index.html's scripts ran, in the same document, so a page that writes on load (defaults, a counter, normalising a shape) writes concurrently with migrate.js, and does it with the new version's code on unmigrated documents. On the draft (§8.2 step 2) this only makes the check less faithful: the draft is a copy that is deleted, and steps 3 and 4 load a fresh document, so the migrate-then-tests flow still works for apps that do not write on load; it is not a merge blocker there. On the live run (step 7) a successful migration keeps whatever the page wrote meanwhile, and §8.4's guarantee is stated as fact. The owner chooses: run migrate.js in a document that does not run the app (a daemon-served empty page of the artifact with the bridge, or an inspect flag the bridge honours by not executing the page), or accept it and tell authors that pages must not write on load (system prompt §10, contract).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":596},"end":{"line":598},"content_hash":"fc66ff47dad5aa447908803b4bbfb7dd7dda1a7dac8dbae50c3456e4c38d3766"},"summary":"'Nothing writes meanwhile' does not hold: the inspect view runs the update's own index.html scripts beside migrate.js, on the draft and on the live app","tags":["bundles","status:needs-decision","review:BW","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:09:18.009593Z","id":"eb004749e079121414f150bdd26584163017f816ee2fe4d8b25da5a8a3969105","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c0df38438bdc08693f6636279f9051c1ae5a59eb8a6a981fe409eefda4bbe0d5","summary":"Decided by the coordinator (the owner may overrule): migrate.js runs in a document that does not run the app. Built as the migration view: ?app=1&inspect=1&migrate=1 names the content frame clax-migrate (web/shell/src/view/frame-host.ts frameName, crates/clax-server/src/boot.rs frame_name), and the bridge, the page's first script, writes <plaintext hidden> while the document parses (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts), so none of the app's scripts run. The only daemon change is that frame name; no route is added. §2, §8.2 step 7, §8.3 and §8.4 say so since b78337cd.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:09:18.009680Z","id":"747c113b143cf6d31fd573383c13628974ea151dc9b37a95b160035a649b316d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b78337cd","summary":"Fixed: the migration view runs none of the app's markup (10d6c2bc), and runMigration replaces the run's document before it returns (eedd6072); §8.3 and §8.4 state both (b78337cd). Evidence: web/e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts 'runMigration imports migrate.js and runs it on the page's db, in a page whose own markup never runs' passes in both frame modes (a page writing boot/seen on load leaves it unwritten; npx playwright test e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts: 12 passed).","supersedes":"c0df38438bdc08693f6636279f9051c1ae5a59eb8a6a981fe409eefda4bbe0d5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:10:03.471280Z","id":"d16bb7403b57413620073b8491e85369cf74f687fd4480f2a6e7e547be062b60","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart. Evidence: flutter test test/agent/loop_test.dart test/agent/loop_single_call_test.dart --name bundle: 4 tests pass ('an app from a bundle (yes): other apps left out and unreadable' asserts no other app in the first message, the note present, and no consent asked for a db_get of another app; the single-call test asserts AgentRequest.fromBundle). The constructor call in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart must still pass fromBundle: fromBundleOf(lineageStore) (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/installer.dart).","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b72fbc92","summary":"AgentLoop takes fromBundle (FutureOr<bool> Function(String aid)) and passes it to dataTools, firstChange, firstContinue, change and AgentRequest","supersedes":"cef8501fe768ac1cdc2fb8dd5a7d00175339cd45127a725c91c1ee53e4dd62ed","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:15:53.408277Z","id":"957883a4796cb03ba58c7f655b5371161831913d8eeacfd121ec1233ef4ee980","body":{"detail":"Two gaps in section 8.4's argument. (1) The update sheet is modal over the app, but when the app is open (section 12.1 shows the sheet over whatever screen is up) its page keeps running behind the sheet: onSnapshot listeners fire on migrate.js's writes and a page that saves on change writes old-shaped documents during the live run, and during the restore. The updater should close or unload the app's page view before the snapshot. (2) The snapshot holds owner-level documents only (docs:collections leaves out data/users/<id>/, which the token can neither read nor write, docs/contract.md:650-652), but migrate.js runs with the page's db in the owner's WebView and can write the owner's own data/users/<id>/ documents; the draft's copy leaves them out too, so the check never runs migrate.js on them and a failed live run cannot put them back.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":604},"end":{"line":609},"content_hash":"89b9de8f629af7a09021200d03cd739b4ce7ded4988228da089175b5bb0d0fce"},"summary":"\"Nothing writes meanwhile\" does not hold for an open app page, and the snapshot cannot cover private data/users documents migrate.js may write","tags":["review","bundles","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.141622Z","id":"1615556a4680489ef449c5f9273c9021a212533afc9f11845063947afee751dc","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"957883a4796cb03ba58c7f655b5371161831913d8eeacfd121ec1233ef4ee980","summary":"Decided by the coordinator (the owner may overrule): during an update the app's page is unloaded behind an Updating cover and the agent is held off (spec §8.4, ac13249e; app.dart 53d79bae). The data/users/ half is not implementable with today's API: the token cannot read or write data/users/<id>/ documents (docs/contract.md, The db tools), so the snapshot cannot include them; §8.4 now says so, and record below asks how to proceed.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:30:15.141883Z","id":"c722cf672571cf9033d9fec261a4f02aeb147c675e11b2ba11d69808bdeb2559","body":{"detail":"The token cannot read or write data/users/<id>/ (docs/contract.md, The db tools), and DocSnapshots (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart) reads through the token, so a failed live migration rolls back owner-level documents only. Options: a migration-view host method that snapshots and restores the page's own data/users documents through its db (web/bridge, lib/agent/inspector.dart), a daemon route letting the owner's token reach its own viewer's documents, or accept the gap (a migration rarely writes per-viewer data in a single-person app).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":607},"end":{"line":609},"content_hash":"f96632c2028defbd63ecfe15299afb07693ccafbbdf2caadfae8ec33fa48e1f2"},"summary":"A live migrate.js's writes to the person's private data/users/<id>/ documents are not snapshotted or restored","tags":["status:needs-decision","bundles","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:33:37.463754Z","id":"716d8e5965a4390f6ef1e0126739a9d90043069b0f2f424c1503670b17b07e2f","body":{"detail":"The page's db reaches documents only at paths it names: GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/docs needs a collection (ListQuery.collection, crates/clax-server/src/routes/docs.rs:189-197), and the only listing of collections, docs:collections (docs.rs:414-434), is token-only and leaves data/users/<id>/ out. db.d.ts (web/contract/0.2.61/db.d.ts) has no collection listing. So Inspector.userDocs(url) has nothing to list from without a daemon change. Options: (1) a write journal in the migration view: web/bridge/src/harness.ts hands migrate.js a db wrapper that reads each document before its first write or delete and sends {path, before} to the host, which Dart syncs to the snapshot before acknowledging, so the run can be undone exactly (covers data/users and owner documents alike; a host round trip per first write); (2) a daemon route or a docs:collections variant for the viewer's own subtree (excluded by the decision); (3) accept the gap as recorded.","kind":"comment","references":"c722cf672571cf9033d9fec261a4f02aeb147c675e11b2ba11d69808bdeb2559","summary":"The page runtime cannot enumerate the viewer's data/users documents, so a snapshot through the migration view cannot be taken as decided","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:50:35.445253Z","id":"32edb986ca1eba939c98e6e6435e430e212c0cc2301f557646c61178fd21d590","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c722cf672571cf9033d9fec261a4f02aeb147c675e11b2ba11d69808bdeb2559","summary":"Decided by the coordinator (the owner may overrule): journal the live migration's writes in the migration view; the token snapshot stays the authority for owner documents and the journal covers data/users/ (and cross-checks the rest).","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:50:35.445454Z","id":"9e5375cc732766775cce8dd48ebad2f46a6a6ce231912f1a2d3207c020f54223","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/caps/db.ts journals each document's first write (2f496eb0); web/shell/src/app/host.ts posts journal and waits for journalAck, restoreJournal replays in reverse; Inspector.runMigration(onWrite) and restoreWrites (db6cc7d8); DocSnapshots.journal syncs each entry before the ack, Updater._replayPrivate replays on rollback and at start (2e2bc3d0). Evidence: npx playwright test e2e/inspect-tests.spec.ts: 14 passed, including 'a journaled migration that fails part way is put back from its journal, the viewer's data/users documents included' in both frame modes; npx vitest run shell bridge: 1233 passed; flutter test test/bundle/ test/app_bundles_test.dart test/agent/ test/ui/host_protocol_test.dart test/ui/inspector_surface_test.dart test/ui/app_screen_test.dart test/ui/bundle_flows_test.dart: +941 ~4, all passed (updater_safety_test 'a failed live migration puts back the person's data/users documents from its journal...'). Spec §8.4 updated in 5dfb922a.","kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2e2bc3d0","summary":"The live migrate.js run is journaled and a rollback replays the journal's data/users entries through the migration view","supersedes":"c722cf672571cf9033d9fec261a4f02aeb147c675e11b2ba11d69808bdeb2559","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:43:57.524959Z","id":"fd9ecc43bb3cddbf23d637783d955fb4f7b6a0bf2888c4f7e4facd768dc430af","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f585f63eb035eabc9a041442847db6819b2b091091ac5b35bf07669c1e8c6e86","summary":"On flutter-app at 9e20d844 (gate fix 2a only after), quality_gates.sh time to usable failed subdomain in all three tries (comment ready 91-102 ms against 86, cold ready latency 39-40 against 38; sandbox passed on retry), and npm run perf alone failed the same way (comment ready 102-103, cold ready latency 40-41; sandbox passed). Logs: target/round5-gates2.log, target/round5-perf-alone.log. Now fails consistently, not now and then.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-06-toolpath-audit-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:21:46.336918Z","id":"30c2de408d9d88bf96148f41cf1c38d568dc9395e317d2e36d2f390db41ca5fb","body":{"detail":"2026-10-16, load average 6-10, debug daemons, web/perf/usable.perf.ts's sample() reproduced with timing hooks (scratch spec, not committed), 7 samples per config, interleaved over 3 rounds. Median subdomain comment ready: flutter-app (daemon+web/dist) 103-106 ms; flutter-app daemon with d4c9fb08's web/dist 102-106; d4c9fb08 daemon+web 101-106; 527db6cf daemon+web (which read 81-83 on 2026-10-09) 89-103. Breakdown, flutter-app, ms from the shell's time origin: Comment button attached and enabled 30-31; Playwright's waitFor+click(force) lands the click at 59-65 (harness round trips into a busy renderer); the frame receives clax:comment-mode at 100-106 and shows the crosshair within 1 ms. The bridge's comment part has loaded by 54, so it is not on the path. Sending clax:comment-mode synchronously from ArtifactController.toggleComment instead of from the afterPaint reaction pass (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:500) changed nothing (101-104 vs 102-104). A Chrome trace of the click shows the shell's handler done 0.5 ms after the click, then one cc ScheduledActionSendBeginMainFrame task on CrRendererMain lasting 32 ms, ~30 ms of it untraced idle before UpdateLayoutTree/Paint; the subdomain frame shares that renderer (*.localhost is same-site), so the message waits for it. --disable-gpu-vsync --disable-frame-rate-limit lowers it only to 95-100. The regression against the 2026-10-01 baseline (56) is shared by every build tested and lives in the browser's frame pacing on this machine, not in a feature, so the limit was not raised. Decision for the owner: re-record the darwin-arm64 baseline on today's machine (CLAX_PERF_RECORD=baseline after removing the entry; budgetFor(105) gives a subdomain commentReady budget of 135 ms), or keep 86 and accept this gate failing here until the pacing is understood.","kind":"comment","ref":"git:f68c3c77","references":"4000ca14d6ad2b689b988bc7a4c84279aa590a81cad5f1bb3201dc72d0d1212b","summary":"Subdomain comment ready reads the same ~100-105 ms on flutter-app, on main's merge-base d4c9fb08 and on the 2026-10-09 main 527db6cf; the time is Chromium frame scheduling and harness latency, not code on this branch","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:30:18.653521Z","id":"7bb9e33b4819a506d7c31a443294bf99989942a95e1cad343a6703ae42ca982e","body":{"detail":"Spike harness target/ios-spike/app on \"Clax iPhone\" (iPhone 17, iOS 26.5 23F77), Info.plist ATS = {NSAllowsLocalNetworking: true} only. Command: xcrun simctl launch --console-pty <udid> dev.empathic.clax.spike -ClaxMode probe. Output (Documents/result.txt): \"step 1 response 200 for http://127.0.0.1:58725/healthz\", \"step 1 loaded: ... {\\\"pid\\\":89157,...,\\\"version\\\":\\\"spike\\\"}\", \"step 2 response 200 for http://localhost:58725/healthz\". The PID is the app's own. Results are summarised in this file's §11 \"Run on the simulator, 2026-10-19\".","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1044},"end":{"line":1044},"content_hash":"e6896f8232cefa6c4fda59e558131c7473ef17e1328e8dd00daf5ea8101a2454"},"summary":"Simulator, iOS 26.5: WKWebView loads http://127.0.0.1:<port>/ and http://localhost:<port>/ under ATS with NSAllowsLocalNetworking alone","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:30:18.653650Z","id":"29746e4734da7d56dc1e2a7b7c3a82089d78fb7b1401d426a60a8cb323382386","body":{"detail":"Screenshot after the first launch of the as-built spike (xcrun simctl io <udid> screenshot target/ios/shots/spike-healthz.png) shows only the /healthz JSON, no system alert; the same for the framed page (target/ios/shots/spike-picker.png before the tap). The app declares no NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription. Because the simulator is not known to show this prompt at all, the check moves to a release device build (Group B), where rules_flutter adds no Dart VM service keys.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1045},"end":{"line":1045},"content_hash":"676ce3e64d1458c54746f7602672078df36c7e41bf3f6e7111386078592e0043"},"summary":"Simulator, iOS 26.5: no local network prompt for loopback; the simulator may not enforce local network privacy, so the release device build still checks it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:30:18.653712Z","id":"3ea21825194362d0de32cf1053e5974c508677816fb63d2f6bcc5bb10fb9ed2f","body":{"detail":"With ATS = {NSAllowsLocalNetworking: true}: \"step 3 failed provisional: Error Domain=NSURLErrorDomain Code=-1022 \\\"The resource could not be loaded because the App Transport Security policy requires the use of a secure connection.\\\" ... NSErrorFailingURLKey=http://spike.localhost:58725/healthz\". The framed page's iframe at http://spike.localhost:<port>/frame was never requested. With NSExceptionDomains = {localhost: {NSIncludesSubdomains: true, NSExceptionAllowsInsecureHTTPLoads: true}} added (target/ios-spike/app/build-sim3): \"step 3 response 200 for http://spike.localhost:58858/healthz\" from the daemon, and the frame server logged \"GET /frame HTTP/1.1 Host: spike.localhost:58887\". So the clax-artifact: scheme fallback of §2.9 is not needed; the ATS key is (see the needs-decision record on §2.9).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1046},"end":{"line":1046},"content_hash":"ea8ce09fc5ef58ad58a44b6151c17ce3ab6bb49e64416e8592226f7aa80812a6"},"summary":"Simulator, iOS 26.5: WebKit resolves *.localhost to loopback, but ATS refuses it under NSAllowsLocalNetworking alone (-1022); with an NSExceptionDomains entry for localhost and its subdomains it loads","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:30:18.653765Z","id":"51b01e8b8fe5928f2995d9dcf4f29b365a07aae7655d99183d7b2b23e409cdf6","body":{"detail":"Failure: an artifact origin http://<id>.localhost:<port>/ fails to load (NSURLErrorDomain -1022) in an app whose Info.plist has only NSAppTransportSecurity › NSAllowsLocalNetworking, measured on the iOS 26.5 simulator (§11 \"Run on the simulator, 2026-10-19\", item 3). Options: (a) add NSExceptionDomains › localhost › {NSIncludesSubdomains: true, NSExceptionAllowsInsecureHTTPLoads: true}, proven to load *.localhost from the in-process daemon; Apple lists NSExceptionAllowsInsecureHTTPLoads among the keys App Review may ask a justification for (loopback-only content served by the app's own process), so the review notes gain a line; (b) the clax-artifact: scheme served by a WKURLSchemeHandler, not designed, a larger change to origins, cookies and the shell. Task 10's Info.plist and the App Review notes depend on the choice; the daemon crate (phase 2) does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":306},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"2046e0d256930be4f4d665917996bf7a417804e6b50d4a1e4fd2be48b5168f7b"},"summary":"§2.9 is wrong that NSAllowsLocalNetworking covers *.localhost: iOS 26.5's ATS refuses http://<id>.localhost:<port>/ with -1022 unless localhost is an exception domain with subdomains and insecure HTTP loads","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:30:18.653814Z","id":"ce4b8ff371e9ee9fbe1f91268cb2579a234c7de04908351b584b6b7b2faf6c7e","body":{"detail":"Parent http://127.0.0.1:<daemon port>/ (loadHTMLString with that base URL) frames http://spike.localhost:<port>/frame; the frame's button posts {kind:'pick'} to the parent, whose message listener calls click() on a hidden <input type=file>. An XCUITest tap (target/ios-spike/uitest, xcodebuild test ... -only-testing:SpikeUITests/SpikeUITests/testFramedTap, TEST SUCCEEDED) logged \"message from http://spike.localhost:60941 frame active=true parent active=true\" then \"input.click() returned\", and iOS showed its file menu (Photo Library, Take Photo or Video, Choose File) over the page (target/ios/shots/spike-picker.png). The frame is cross-origin to the parent, as an artifact is to the shell.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":764},"end":{"line":772},"content_hash":"243e9f655df33dd4b07c286f93d987e7011523d9b013c3ff3da417d243a27583"},"summary":"Simulator, iOS 26.5: a tap in a cross-origin frame lets the top document open the file picker through input.click() on a postMessage","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:30:18.653860Z","id":"f68a72c92ff8a769254dbec6a3767e565f7886d0ea147bca7c75bc119ef8f35a","body":{"detail":"xcrun simctl launch <udid> com.apple.Preferences put the spike in the background (\"13.274 sceneDidEnterBackground: clax_state=2\"); after 60 s, curl -m 5 http://127.0.0.1:61479/healthz timed out (exit 28: the process was suspended). xcrun simctl launch <udid> dev.empathic.clax.spike brought back PID 4208: \"85.308 willEnterForeground: clax_state=2; reloading /healthz\", \"85.632 step 1 response 200 for http://127.0.0.1:61479/healthz\"; curl then answered 200 with pid 4208. Log: target/ios/spike-run/run5-bg-steps.log. A listener reclaimed by iOS on a device is not exercised by the simulator.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1047},"end":{"line":1048},"content_hash":"d1c7b62d5bb6a2d3c99eefc2953066c8d54e45b76b77c6041d5caac22b1b3c7b"},"summary":"Simulator, iOS 26.5: the daemon's listener answered after a 72 s background cycle, same PID and port; the simulator suspended the app but did not reclaim the socket","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:30:18.653907Z","id":"7b458ad9493b2a198dce0c41023c57a3f7267dc02bf2b0f70d1fb6b414aadf77","body":{"detail":"From Documents/result.txt of six launches: clax_start took 0.058, 0.067, 0.012, 0.071, 0.032 s on later launches (0.157 s from launch to port on the first, as-built launch); \"loaded\" at 2.126 s (first launch, WebKit processes cold), then 1.135, 1.201, 1.104, 1.792 (under XCUITest), 1.281 s. Logs: target/ios/spike-run/*-result.txt.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1049},"end":{"line":1049},"content_hash":"f482ba7f7f658ec8731fdf35cd95b89277f709827abe74db40bd052b885c4130"},"summary":"Simulator, iOS 26.5: clax_start(0) returns in 12–71 ms; /healthz loads 2.13 s after the first launch after install and 1.10–1.79 s after later launches","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:21:02.472405Z","id":"963a1799ebd99f0197ae7e6ea38456eb45fbfff146af49cf15da31305176b7e1","body":{"detail":"No NSAllowsArbitraryLoads (ios_app_test fails on it). Changing the decision means editing that one NSAppTransportSecurity dict and the three ATS checks in apps/clax_app/tool/ios-app-check.sh.","kind":"comment","references":"51b01e8b8fe5928f2995d9dcf4f29b365a07aae7655d99183d7b2b23e409cdf6","span":{"start":{"line":306},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"2046e0d256930be4f4d665917996bf7a417804e6b50d4a1e4fd2be48b5168f7b"},"summary":"Interim: apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Info.plist:24-45 ships option (a), NSAllowsLocalNetworking plus NSExceptionDomains › localhost › {NSIncludesSubdomains, NSExceptionAllowsInsecureHTTPLoads}, and //apps/clax_app:ios_app_test checks both; the choice stays open here","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:02.421075Z","id":"d32741a11b7448d12bea5790a01d7dd16774da79eae11ad9a2bdd1a94d11d28b","body":{"detail":"Owner's decision 3 (a longer build pauses and resumes on return) was answered again for open question 4 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md:1207-1210). The pause is AppPresence.pause in apps/clax_app/lib/platform/network_pause.dart, called from AppRoot._pauseRuns in apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart on BackgroundWork.stopped where pausesRuns.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":617},"end":{"line":622},"content_hash":"356f8b94b4ed7625d8b989f91e2c2a343564b0608740f5e51a5f68d4ad770866"},"summary":"BGContinuedProcessingTask (iOS 26) would let a long build finish in the background with a system progress UI; not used: the owner chose pause and resume","tags":["revisit:after-testflight-feedback","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-professional-ui-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:09:58.230454Z","id":"7a54de4565d81fa5f46cffc42a35b1c73399364203721ebe8372e5fb95383698","body":{"detail":"A WebView sidebar gives no source-list selection, type-select, outline semantics, sidebar material or native menus, and a broken home app (failed, being updated, or changed by the agent) would break the window's navigation. The sidebar is native Flutter (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/split/sidebar.dart), fed by HomeHost and layout/main through HomeLayout, so a comment on the home app cannot reshape it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":497},"content_hash":"5e65c08b41d27e7df7dd9388d6922d1222c2c7da156518cb0e2636211886d6ad"},"summary":"The home app rendered in the sidebar was not taken","tags":["macos","revisit:people ask to change the sidebar by commenting","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361509Z","id":"5c5fe78b8c41dc403e8c7f2e1b570bf4bb4f5a208b50e0ec4e9d649220596c9c","body":{"detail":"Rejected: a listener in the app is reachable by every other app on the device, so it needs the token, key cookie and Host checks (docs/contract.md Security model) the scheme makes unnecessary; it keeps a port, health checks and restarts after iOS reclaims the socket (iOS spec Review Focus 1), and its WebViews depend on ATS and cleartext exceptions. clax-embed's call reaches the same router (crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:707 build_router) with no socket.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":183},"content_hash":"3f6379bb43b223bcfca149b9e8ce365719c49ff69336bbea0abb9894df2e2493"},"summary":"Keep loopback HTTP inside the app's process (clax-ios's shape on all three platforms) instead of feeding requests to the router with no socket","tags":["revisit:a platform WebView cannot answer a custom scheme with real origins (Task 13's spike fails on Apple), or the app must serve other devices on the LAN","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361605Z","id":"317676a6511299de89562a65cf27b8c204d95069698fcdee9c6d55da4ce8b1e4","body":{"detail":"Rejected for now: the agent (apps/clax_app/lib/agent, 41 files, 16,662 lines: tool loop, tools, prompts, the Messages API and claude CLI backends) is Dart and tested; a port is a rewrite with no user-visible gain while Clax's own agent is app-only. What localhost and the Worker need (durable steps, publish checks) moves to the core (§8) so a later Rust agent finds them there.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":519},"end":{"line":564},"content_hash":"c696664cb2a4ab970c0d8f3b8f49b609aa9b9abb9259a470fea23a8686b1b48d"},"summary":"Run the queue and the agent in Rust inside clax-embed, so localhost and the hosted Worker could run Clax's own agent too","tags":["revisit:Clax's own agent is wanted on localhost (clax serve) or on the hosted Worker","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361657Z","id":"480359322c585262d4037e1760df8c77cae9fe608dfe268b83e28df77ebd5927","body":{"detail":"Rejected: a Dart store cannot commit a step in the same transaction as the version it publishes, which is what removes the change ledger's unknowns (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/ledger.dart); it would be a second SQLite in the process with its own migrations and backups; and outside agents' and the Worker's publishes would not see it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":629},"end":{"line":724},"content_hash":"3681d0272240903a7cffcac4f98f28d0b480bafc44d87182b50e7fc1e908164c"},"summary":"Keep the queue's durable state in a Dart-side store (SQLite via a Dart package, or the JSON files) instead of core tables","tags":["revisit:jobs must survive without the core (e.g. queued while the core cannot open), or the core's write load from job updates shows in just perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361707Z","id":"c1083d29075e964851cab10e3e5a72a9b6f234c56f46b70b14aec07f760de85b","body":{"detail":"Rejected: flutter_rust_bridge generates unsafe code and its own exports across the crate, which the no-unsafe rule (AGENTS.md, scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh) could not bound to named functions; it adds a codegen step to Bazel and pub/crate dependencies for an ABI of four functions carrying opaque frames.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":233},"content_hash":"b4cad7b44bf89c8a7520b7a623a4003670f2563efc1fd6ce9b23dfb54c98a4e2"},"summary":"Generate the Dart and Rust bindings with flutter_rust_bridge instead of a hand-written four-function C ABI","tags":["revisit:the ABI grows past about ten functions or needs typed structs across the boundary","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361752Z","id":"bfe57594cea11c90bae56eb0d5a33943b9a1ae558c950da4d16f0fdc1e2dcd38","body":{"detail":"Rejected: bytes must cross the boundary for every call; with scalar-only exports they would go through the filesystem or a second channel, slower and harder to make atomic. Two pointer arguments, each read by exactly one std::slice::from_raw_parts behind a // SAFETY: comment, are the smallest unsafe surface that carries bytes; scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh pins it line by line (§14).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":184},"end":{"line":233},"content_hash":"b4cad7b44bf89c8a7520b7a623a4003670f2563efc1fd6ce9b23dfb54c98a4e2"},"summary":"Keep scalar-only exports (clax-ios's rule: u16/i32 arguments) and pass request and response bytes some other way, e.g. through files or a Dart-allocated buffer index","tags":["revisit:Dart gains a safe way to hand a Rust function a byte slice without a raw pointer","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361796Z","id":"983dd2ee106e5d91f5aa81b96a3f680dde51c6ce1d40aa45faecfac4710f8230","body":{"detail":"Not taken: long polls (pollFeedback's ?wait=, waitQuestion) and multi-second publishes would hold a pool isolate each, and a call from the UI isolate (the WebView relay) would block frames; posting the response to a Dart port removes both and makes free unnecessary.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"f02a8bdc95cd8741a5e9f233c17b8d30c2c7120ece06dcbd3b0ffbb0ac87eb2f"},"summary":"A blocking clax_embed_call that returns its response buffer, freed by clax_embed_free, run from a pool of helper isolates","tags":["revisit:Dart FFI gains asynchronous native calls, or the owner prefers the five-function shape as written","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361841Z","id":"2862f97f70dfa4cd797802ccc94f0b6f765fe6e384596d152ed093652d45d09a","body":{"detail":"Not taken: every WebView feature the app uses (navigation delegate, channels, snapshots, cookies, the inspector) is built on webview_flutter; a second WebView stack would duplicate it. A registration hook is a small patch carried in bazel/flutter/plugin_overlays.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":404},"end":{"line":434},"content_hash":"1dbe13ee8f1bc1363b88db22e21f0e22bfe025445513ebdb8d047f87cc5a5e7e"},"summary":"Give the shell its own platform view (a WKWebView the runner creates with Clax's scheme handler) instead of patching webview_flutter_wkwebview","tags":["revisit:webview_flutter_wkwebview changes its configuration code so the patch no longer applies cheaply, or upstream adds a scheme-handler API","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361882Z","id":"ed5b4750dbb76b026c8f4464a628110e130f76082d742b32cea7b03a0a08d036","body":{"detail":"Not taken by default: the inspect view, capture and inspector live in Flutter platform views (lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart), which need an attached FlutterView; an offscreen path is a second renderer to keep equal to the first.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"d0aa439d53e11b59abc4c7c536ea6381f0e0b33ae678bec955fa48df73e942d0"},"summary":"On a WorkManager wake with no UI, render in an offscreen native Android WebView so the job finishes without the person opening Clax","tags":["revisit:kill-and-resume on the owner's phone shows jobs commonly stranded at a render after a wake","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361923Z","id":"9afee9fe262a9e3ae509befd444cebba1833bfff814451250d8e6924778c5a65","body":{"detail":"Decision 2 names open, call(request bytes) -> response bytes, free, close and subscribe. This spec takes S1: call posts the response to a Dart port because routes the app uses wait (GET /api/sessions/{sid}/feedback?wait=, waitQuestion) and large publishes take seconds, which a blocking call would hold on an isolate's thread. Options: (a) S1 as written; (b) a blocking call plus free, run from a pool of helper isolates.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":83},"end":{"line":93},"content_hash":"f02a8bdc95cd8741a5e9f233c17b8d30c2c7120ece06dcbd3b0ffbb0ac87eb2f"},"summary":"Owner decision: may call answer through a Dart port (four functions: open, call, subscribe, close) instead of returning response bytes freed by free?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.361966Z","id":"03c1a3da6e1567504b4a6e105a866b0980e41092ac49825251588887dfc7b36b","body":{"detail":"There is no WorkManager in the app today (apps/clax_app/android has none). Rendering needs a Flutter platform view. Options: (a) S6 as written; (b) render offscreen natively (the alternative recorded on these lines); (c) no WorkManager wake at all, resume only at launch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"d0aa439d53e11b59abc4c7c536ea6381f0e0b33ae678bec955fa48df73e942d0"},"summary":"Owner decision: a WorkManager wake runs a job only until it needs a render, then pauses it with 'Open Clax to keep building <title>'","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.362006Z","id":"612c5e1ba2e12b711de4009903694b685cabf7105c9ca9b82e6983c4a563dffe","body":{"detail":"Decision 6 mentions an existing BGProcessingTask; none exists (apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift uses beginBackgroundTask only; the iOS spec turned down BGContinuedProcessingTask). Options: (a) none, as S7 says; (b) register a BGProcessingTask that resumes open jobs when iOS grants time (needs a headless Flutter engine on iOS, as S6 on Android).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":125},"content_hash":"706abd7ee65cbb13d9ca7d11387ca8233d1a4b7273bcf133d3de800f525bda09"},"summary":"Owner decision: no BGProcessingTask on iOS; jobs paused by the OS resume at the next launch","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.362046Z","id":"9a7b1941d0d01a046296d64a7f1e8944bd43951be16af7667384656c1ba43164","body":{"detail":"main's crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs ends at 40 with different 39 and 40 than this branch's (which end at 43; this spec adds 44). Installed homes on the owner's phone and Mac are at this branch's 43. Whichever numbering the merge keeps needs a schema-based adoption step for the other (adopt_earlier_flutter_app, crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1307) and a backup, tested on a fixture of each.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":818},"end":{"line":821},"content_hash":"3945cb80abe09a59eb26e9e69fff07f87927da1da1a98b247c5616bf3e8ec527"},"summary":"Owner decision: the migration numbering between this branch (39-43 app migrations, 44 jobs) and main (its own 39 and 40) at merge","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:34:55.362087Z","id":"4139ec080443f50e394fafd86f827b771a340ac344e62547b15a647355c49b30","body":{"detail":"The old port was kept across starts (<support>/daemon-port), so pages that kept state in localStorage rather than their documents had it. Carrying it would need each old origin loaded once over a loopback listener, which decision 1 forbids. Options: (a) accept the one-time loss; (b) a one-time migration build that still has the listener.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":843},"end":{"line":855},"content_hash":"b07b06f7e67eb58a364efef52e36702d10f09e333cc88a54438514b154ee4dff"},"summary":"Owner decision: is losing pages' localStorage on the old http://<id>.localhost:<port> origins acceptable when the app moves to the scheme?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.475654Z","id":"03248ace6a53313aef335ae89f6e19242971c5752c83c3a817a96fc87d1e46e5","body":{"detail":"Rejected: a listener in the app is reachable by every other app on the device, so it needs the token, key cookie and Host checks (docs/contract.md Security model) the scheme makes unnecessary; it keeps a port, health checks and restarts after iOS reclaims the socket (iOS spec Review Focus 1), and its WebViews depend on ATS and cleartext exceptions. clax-embed's call reaches the same router (crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:707 build_router) with no socket.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":184},"content_hash":"712fe4ac4272580623d37a16faf26aca907358e85c19dbd60242dfdc792553c9"},"summary":"Keep loopback HTTP inside the app's process (clax-ios's shape on all three platforms) instead of feeding requests to the router with no socket","supersedes":"5c5fe78b8c41dc403e8c7f2e1b570bf4bb4f5a208b50e0ec4e9d649220596c9c","tags":["revisit:a platform WebView cannot answer a custom scheme with real origins (Task 13's spike fails on Apple), or the app must serve other devices on the LAN","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.527468Z","id":"e227004b85acc8c6b5709dac29228912c2b8eb0558fa37f0adfbd599165b19b6","body":{"detail":"Rejected: bytes must cross the boundary for every call; with scalar-only exports they would go through the filesystem or a second channel, slower and harder to make atomic. Two pointer arguments, each read by exactly one std::slice::from_raw_parts behind a // SAFETY: comment, are the smallest unsafe surface that carries bytes; scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh pins it line by line (§14).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"b4cad7b44bf89c8a7520b7a623a4003670f2563efc1fd6ce9b23dfb54c98a4e2"},"summary":"Keep scalar-only exports (clax-ios's rule: u16/i32 arguments) and pass request and response bytes some other way, e.g. through files or a Dart-allocated buffer index","supersedes":"bfe57594cea11c90bae56eb0d5a33943b9a1ae558c950da4d16f0fdc1e2dcd38","tags":["revisit:Dart gains a safe way to hand a Rust function a byte slice without a raw pointer","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.576152Z","id":"95a064dc1fad56331dc20b7b7eb21c95ac85555e4028135b40cc7ab2da682b8a","body":{"detail":"Rejected: flutter_rust_bridge generates unsafe code and its own exports across the crate, which the no-unsafe rule (AGENTS.md, scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh) could not bound to named functions; it adds a codegen step to Bazel and pub/crate dependencies for an ABI of four functions carrying opaque frames.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":185},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"b4cad7b44bf89c8a7520b7a623a4003670f2563efc1fd6ce9b23dfb54c98a4e2"},"summary":"Generate the Dart and Rust bindings with flutter_rust_bridge instead of a hand-written four-function C ABI","supersedes":"c1083d29075e964851cab10e3e5a72a9b6f234c56f46b70b14aec07f760de85b","tags":["revisit:the ABI grows past about ten functions or needs typed structs across the boundary","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.624959Z","id":"741ec62b5ec295647a39191afe03b494b5c6ea98cf9799ca99e28df08cefaf7f","body":{"detail":"Not taken: every WebView feature the app uses (navigation delegate, channels, snapshots, cookies, the inspector) is built on webview_flutter; a second WebView stack would duplicate it. A registration hook is a small patch carried in bazel/flutter/plugin_overlays.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":411},"end":{"line":441},"content_hash":"1dbe13ee8f1bc1363b88db22e21f0e22bfe025445513ebdb8d047f87cc5a5e7e"},"summary":"Give the shell its own platform view (a WKWebView the runner creates with Clax's scheme handler) instead of patching webview_flutter_wkwebview","supersedes":"2862f97f70dfa4cd797802ccc94f0b6f765fe6e384596d152ed093652d45d09a","tags":["revisit:webview_flutter_wkwebview changes its configuration code so the patch no longer applies cheaply, or upstream adds a scheme-handler API","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.676009Z","id":"c893bf2565d2d3b8cc306a9a899f68d239d35e69b5ba0c30a5ccc70b3be87775","body":{"detail":"Rejected for now: the agent (apps/clax_app/lib/agent, 41 files, 16,662 lines: tool loop, tools, prompts, the Messages API and claude CLI backends) is Dart and tested; a port is a rewrite with no user-visible gain while Clax's own agent is app-only. What localhost and the Worker need (durable steps, publish checks) moves to the core (§8) so a later Rust agent finds them there.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":542},"end":{"line":651},"content_hash":"a26f1e0396a53b7696f2eb7457cb0831115ad33ee09940b88ea12c4ccb49edb7"},"summary":"Run the queue and the agent in Rust inside clax-embed, so localhost and the hosted Worker could run Clax's own agent too","supersedes":"317676a6511299de89562a65cf27b8c204d95069698fcdee9c6d55da4ce8b1e4","tags":["revisit:Clax's own agent is wanted on localhost (clax serve) or on the hosted Worker","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.727384Z","id":"8d37604b3a5f85acfc5f58a12348d1fee7f8def942747be8b49263d47da0e1e7","body":{"detail":"Rejected: a Dart store cannot commit a step in the same transaction as the version it publishes, which is what removes the change ledger's unknowns (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/ledger.dart); it would be a second SQLite in the process with its own migrations and backups; and outside agents' and the Worker's publishes would not see it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":652},"end":{"line":754},"content_hash":"d1295756292146ff5cae620e6ea3d3924f80ce06c26e9a62df1f0e5f9f91f086"},"summary":"Keep the queue's durable state in a Dart-side store (SQLite via a Dart package, or the JSON files) instead of core tables","supersedes":"480359322c585262d4037e1760df8c77cae9fe608dfe268b83e28df77ebd5927","tags":["revisit:jobs must survive without the core (e.g. queued while the core cannot open), or the core's write load from job updates shows in just perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.778556Z","id":"577508d2b66be6d11fd728f43fedbfb94c35e79fdf72c6a6f804b445882cebd5","body":{"detail":"main's crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs ends at 40 with different 39 and 40 than this branch's (which end at 43; this spec adds 44). Installed homes on the owner's phone and Mac are at this branch's 43. Whichever numbering the merge keeps needs a schema-based adoption step for the other (adopt_earlier_flutter_app, crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1307) and a backup, tested on a fixture of each.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":848},"end":{"line":851},"content_hash":"3945cb80abe09a59eb26e9e69fff07f87927da1da1a98b247c5616bf3e8ec527"},"summary":"Owner decision: the migration numbering between this branch (39-43 app migrations, 44 jobs) and main (its own 39 and 40) at merge","supersedes":"9a7b1941d0d01a046296d64a7f1e8944bd43951be16af7667384656c1ba43164","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T01:47:16.827913Z","id":"0b01a4c0446061f19449891aeccd2d80bbbf63b413063ae9f2f41efc2ab0a84f","body":{"detail":"The old port was kept across starts (<support>/daemon-port), so pages that kept state in localStorage rather than their documents had it. Carrying it would need each old origin loaded once over a loopback listener, which decision 1 forbids. Options: (a) accept the one-time loss; (b) a one-time migration build that still has the listener.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":873},"end":{"line":885},"content_hash":"b07b06f7e67eb58a364efef52e36702d10f09e333cc88a54438514b154ee4dff"},"summary":"Owner decision: is losing pages' localStorage on the old http://<id>.localhost:<port> origins acceptable when the app moves to the scheme?","supersedes":"4139ec080443f50e394fafd86f827b771a340ac344e62547b15a647355c49b30","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:42.832825Z","id":"c5c6d942414be3e90b75486a92c700de64e8084dc7d5fb4a892f461fa00fc432","body":{"detail":"Not taken: long polls (pollFeedback's ?wait=, waitQuestion) and multi-second publishes would hold a pool isolate each, and a call from the UI isolate (the WebView relay) would block frames; posting the response to a Dart port removes both and makes free unnecessary.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"f02a8bdc95cd8741a5e9f233c17b8d30c2c7120ece06dcbd3b0ffbb0ac87eb2f"},"summary":"A blocking clax_embed_call that returns its response buffer, freed by clax_embed_free, run from a pool of helper isolates","supersedes":"983dd2ee106e5d91f5aa81b96a3f680dde51c6ce1d40aa45faecfac4710f8230","tags":["revisit:Dart FFI gains asynchronous native calls, or the owner prefers the five-function shape as written","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:42.882889Z","id":"3b57bf4e47ccb181a072298e7e414a5cf07b7239a855c2eab365755bc3928a87","body":{"detail":"Decision 2 names open, call(request bytes) -> response bytes, free, close and subscribe. This spec takes S1: call posts the response to a Dart port because routes the app uses wait (GET /api/sessions/{sid}/feedback?wait=, waitQuestion) and large publishes take seconds, which a blocking call would hold on an isolate's thread. Options: (a) S1 as written; (b) a blocking call plus free, run from a pool of helper isolates.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"f02a8bdc95cd8741a5e9f233c17b8d30c2c7120ece06dcbd3b0ffbb0ac87eb2f"},"summary":"Owner decision: may call answer through a Dart port (four functions: open, call, subscribe, close) instead of returning response bytes freed by free?","supersedes":"9afee9fe262a9e3ae509befd444cebba1833bfff814451250d8e6924778c5a65","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:42.931474Z","id":"20ce516532f5503ed04a45b56a4fbe4eb5c9b60255b7a8a7c603c2d752cd0fc1","body":{"detail":"Decision 6 mentions an existing BGProcessingTask; none exists (apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift uses beginBackgroundTask only; the iOS spec turned down BGContinuedProcessingTask). Options: (a) none, as S7 says; (b) register a BGProcessingTask that resumes open jobs when iOS grants time (needs a headless Flutter engine on iOS, as S6 on Android).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"706abd7ee65cbb13d9ca7d11387ca8233d1a4b7273bcf133d3de800f525bda09"},"summary":"Owner decision: no BGProcessingTask on iOS; jobs paused by the OS resume at the next launch","supersedes":"612c5e1ba2e12b711de4009903694b685cabf7105c9ca9b82e6983c4a563dffe","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
