{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.076766Z","id":"95c707ad3b788bcb6145548a1d353fd31b1c96baff069f09672dd0c8317eba89","body":{"detail":"Rejected: flutter_rust_bridge generates unsafe code and its own exports across the crate, which the no-unsafe rule (AGENTS.md, scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh) could not bound to named functions; it adds a codegen step to Bazel and pub/crate dependencies for an ABI of four functions carrying opaque frames.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"b4cad7b44bf89c8a7520b7a623a4003670f2563efc1fd6ce9b23dfb54c98a4e2"},"summary":"Generate the Dart and Rust bindings with flutter_rust_bridge instead of a hand-written four-function C ABI","supersedes":"95a064dc1fad56331dc20b7b7eb21c95ac85555e4028135b40cc7ab2da682b8a","tags":["revisit:the ABI grows past about ten functions or needs typed structs across the boundary","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.126241Z","id":"8a1ffffcc59c4b643764d10af9f1cd9f6622bdf79f8a7650a7ebfd0c99d43ca4","body":{"detail":"Not taken: every WebView feature the app uses (navigation delegate, channels, snapshots, cookies, the inspector) is built on webview_flutter; a second WebView stack would duplicate it. A registration hook is a small patch carried in bazel/flutter/plugin_overlays.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":446},"end":{"line":476},"content_hash":"1dbe13ee8f1bc1363b88db22e21f0e22bfe025445513ebdb8d047f87cc5a5e7e"},"summary":"Give the shell its own platform view (a WKWebView the runner creates with Clax's scheme handler) instead of patching webview_flutter_wkwebview","supersedes":"741ec62b5ec295647a39191afe03b494b5c6ea98cf9799ca99e28df08cefaf7f","tags":["revisit:webview_flutter_wkwebview changes its configuration code so the patch no longer applies cheaply, or upstream adds a scheme-handler API","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.176147Z","id":"a609c41c36db7202029f258e5de82166dfff03d5adf2925475870ac04e3725bb","body":{"detail":"Rejected for now: the agent (apps/clax_app/lib/agent, 41 files, 16,662 lines: tool loop, tools, prompts, the Messages API and claude CLI backends) is Dart and tested; a port is a rewrite with no user-visible gain while Clax's own agent is app-only. What localhost and the Worker need (durable steps, publish checks) moves to the core (§8) so a later Rust agent finds them there.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":577},"end":{"line":773},"content_hash":"d8ccc4ccc555e12db9918622bef4a66db210c91c0e7bfdb7d64d3c6c4b7c815c"},"summary":"Run the queue and the agent in Rust inside clax-embed, so localhost and the hosted Worker could run Clax's own agent too","supersedes":"c893bf2565d2d3b8cc306a9a899f68d239d35e69b5ba0c30a5ccc70b3be87775","tags":["revisit:Clax's own agent is wanted on localhost (clax serve) or on the hosted Worker","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.225472Z","id":"9b494bb315cf57d4c3404a3eb760a659a9fc1880a3ae78f1822f96a2d6994c31","body":{"detail":"Rejected: a Dart store cannot commit a step in the same transaction as the version it publishes, which is what removes the change ledger's unknowns (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/ledger.dart); it would be a second SQLite in the process with its own migrations and backups; and outside agents' and the Worker's publishes would not see it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":775},"end":{"line":890},"content_hash":"5b14709c5c3a1b8a87f99c36605b935108c8588a8087d01b49f1063059456415"},"summary":"Keep the queue's durable state in a Dart-side store (SQLite via a Dart package, or the JSON files) instead of core tables","supersedes":"8d37604b3a5f85acfc5f58a12348d1fee7f8def942747be8b49263d47da0e1e7","tags":["revisit:jobs must survive without the core (e.g. queued while the core cannot open), or the core's write load from job updates shows in just perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.274467Z","id":"e05463d6bcfbd764396f880bafd173aa8e2b57cf23188d523f2f8cdbc4f0bfb3","body":{"detail":"The old port was kept across starts (<support>/daemon-port), so pages that kept state in localStorage rather than their documents had it. Carrying it would need each old origin loaded once over a loopback listener, which decision 1 forbids. Options: (a) accept the one-time loss; (b) a one-time migration build that still has the listener.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1053},"end":{"line":1064},"content_hash":"7648c7eed7309c5c8f4e884df6c1497ec0cd36b5554d1ae558df409cfdf6f44d"},"summary":"Owner decision: is losing pages' localStorage on the old http://<id>.localhost:<port> origins acceptable when the app moves to the scheme?","supersedes":"0b01a4c0446061f19449891aeccd2d80bbbf63b413063ae9f2f41efc2ab0a84f","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.323878Z","id":"f5d78b7053c312dc95581de9555feb84b7f6f77432ef482d0324010e21359f07","body":{"detail":"The owner chose \"resume at launch; no wake\" on 2026-10-19 (option (c) of this record): no WorkManager wake and no headless engine on Android; jobs resume at the next launch on every platform, and the foreground service keeps running jobs alive on Android as before. The spec says so in S6 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:148-152), decision 12 (:102-104) and §7.6 (:761-771); plan Task 28 (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md) carries no wake.","kind":"comment","references":"03c1a3da6e1567504b4a6e105a866b0980e41092ac49825251588887dfc7b36b","summary":"Decided by the owner on 2026-10-19: resume at launch; no wake","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.324128Z","id":"d08970c1f9abd356bf33362d811ce0d071c2fed95ebf2bb4f42f99ddd5c8f305","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Decided by the owner on 2026-10-19: resume at launch; no wake (spec S6, decision 12, §7.6)","supersedes":"03c1a3da6e1567504b4a6e105a866b0980e41092ac49825251588887dfc7b36b","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.372577Z","id":"810dde95508a0d4108bce08cc7575ec8c5ce7bc3d43a498d641d681c5c598c88","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Obsolete: there is no wake to render in. The owner dropped the WorkManager wake and the headless engine on 2026-10-19 (record 03c1a3da; spec S6 and decision 12), so every render runs with the app's UI.","supersedes":"ed5b4750dbb76b026c8f4464a628110e130f76082d742b32cea7b03a0a08d036","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.422128Z","id":"a3fb87063b4d2cb8e2b033b04f3841983e0082fdaedf7dfe81a5216a50af63a4","body":{"detail":"The owner chose on 2026-10-19 that this branch follows main's numbering (spec decision 13): it takes main's migrations 39 (legal_agreements) and 40 (briefs) verbatim, moves the app's five to 41-45 (APP_MIGRATION = 41), and numbers the jobs migration 46. Installed homes at this branch's old numbering (the owner's phone and Mac, user_version 43 with the app's migrations at 39-43) are recognised by their schema (db_read_grants and questions.thread_id present, none of main's marks above 38) in a fourth layout of adopt_earlier_flutter_app (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1307) with MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38, after the pre-migration backup; they get main's 39 and 40 and user_version 45, and no app migration runs twice. Spec §10.2 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:970-1047) is the design; plan Task 19 implements and tests it on fixtures flutter-app-4508df19f.sql and flutter-app-43.sql.","kind":"comment","references":"577508d2b66be6d11fd728f43fedbfb94c35e79fdf72c6a6f804b445882cebd5","summary":"Decided by the owner on 2026-10-19: follow main's numbering and adopt installed homes by schema","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.422389Z","id":"18c2a26edd0c21da2b7b9446289e3a68544646c10c8307463af198bef6f7535f","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Decided by the owner on 2026-10-19: main's numbering, installed homes adopted by schema after a backup (spec §10.2, plan Task 19)","supersedes":"577508d2b66be6d11fd728f43fedbfb94c35e79fdf72c6a6f804b445882cebd5","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.472488Z","id":"e7c1a8b81f3a26ed512f1bf92ececcbc380007d0981f9c543909da34c5d1cd6a","body":{"detail":"A fifth export would change the four-function ABI and the unsafe check of plan Tasks 7 and 8 (scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh), and would not carry over to the localhost daemon, where an owner is an SSE client. Tying the claim to the claimant's stream needs no new export: a closed Dart port fails the core's next post and ends the subscription, and Hub::nudge makes that post at claim time.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":731},"end":{"line":760},"content_hash":"50d08569e3f1fd555fdb95200b3399beee66381fe2704205530f644262798320"},"summary":"Bind the queue owner claim to a Dart port with a fifth C function (clax_embed_claim) instead of to the claimant's event stream","tags":["revisit:a dead worker's claim is released too late in practice (the new worker waits visibly for owner_held to clear)","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:17:43.472561Z","id":"4a993eb6194869aedfb3bc978379ff90882c4c611b05a10351ecb0e5526890b2","body":{"detail":"The first draft of this spec took leases; the owner chose one in-memory queue owner per client on 2026-10-19 (decision 10): no column, no clock in any job rule, and a claim that dies with its claimant's stream and with the core.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":731},"end":{"line":760},"content_hash":"50d08569e3f1fd555fdb95200b3399beee66381fe2704205530f644262798320"},"summary":"Wall-clock leases on jobs (jobs.lease_until, taken with a revision check and renewed each minute)","tags":["revisit:jobs of one client must run in several processes over one home at once","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:43:09.520603Z","id":"7592d0f23263d907dc0876cf7da82756e702e868275e9255116984625894e7c0","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs: APP_MIGRATION = 41, MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38 (legal_agreements, briefs), adopt_earlier_flutter_app's fourth layout. Main's MIGRATIONS list is a prefix of this branch's (`git show main:crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs | sed -n '/^pub const MIGRATIONS/,/^];/p' | sed '$d'` diffed against the same lines here prints nothing). Passing in //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: migrations::tests::the_app_at_39_to_43_is_adopted_into_mains_numbering, an_adopted_home_is_never_rerun, each_app_prefix_at_the_old_numbering_is_adopted, an_old_numbering_home_whose_marks_disagree_is_refused, a_home_of_this_numbering_is_not_adopted, a_home_at_mains_40_gets_the_apps_migrations_after_a_copy, the_app_migrations_follow_mains_in_this_order. The jobs migration (spec section 10.2) is therefore 46.","kind":"comment","references":"18c2a26edd0c21da2b7b9446289e3a68544646c10c8307463af198bef6f7535f","summary":"Done in 4479a586c: main's 39 and 40 copied verbatim, the app's migrations at 41 to 45, homes at the earlier 39-43 adopted by schema","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:04:06.182383Z","id":"73e25ea57eac7e3e9cceecefb2433280222d99f83bdf795747b13f71b1800ea3","body":{"detail":"Section 4.4 (and plan Task 15, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md:973) has the handler write a fresh clax-nonce into each shell-host HTML answer and give the same one to claxHost.init for that load; it refuses only /a/... outside the main frame. An artifact's content can put <iframe src=\"clax://app/\"> (the gallery, or any non-/a/ shell document) in its page: the handler answers it with a new nonce, and if the surface treats that as the load's nonce it replaces the main frame's, after which the app drops the real shell's messages under its own nonce (a denial of the shell by any artifact). frame-ancestors 'none' does not help: it is applied after the handler has answered. The channel's isMainFrame check keeps the framed shell's posts out, but not the nonce swap. WKURLSchemeTask exposes no frame; Android's WebResourceRequest.isForMainFrame does.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":478},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"b1b0a01cca24d2b7fe439277c4eaa3dd6c953634911707bf7bda7ee2daadc7f3"},"suggested_fix":"Bind the nonce to the main frame's navigation, not to the scheme answer: refuse every shell-host document outside the main frame (Android isForMainFrame; Apple decidePolicyFor navigationAction with targetFrame.isMainFrame, cancelling subframe navigations to the shell host), and have the surface take a nonce only for the main frame's committed navigation. Say so in section 4.4 and plan Task 15, with a spike check that a content frame's iframe of the shell's / is refused.","summary":"The scheme handler mints a nonce for every shell document it answers, a subframe's included, and hands it to claxHost.init: a page that frames a shell URL can make the app take its frame's nonce as the load's","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
